<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jahangir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1569">1569</a>–<a href="/years/1627">1627</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Prince Salim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jahangir was the fourth Mughal emperor, reigning from 1605 to 1627. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a>, born Prince Salim, he largely kept his father's system of government, made peace with Mewar in 1615 and received the English envoy Sir Thomas Roe. A connoisseur of painting and nature, he wrote a candid memoir, while his wife Nur Jahan held great influence at court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jahangir.jpg" alt="Jahangir" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abu al-Hasan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jahangircrop.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
